---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/privy-alternative';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'alternatives/privy-alternative');
const desc = description(site, 'alternatives/privy-alternative');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Should a Privy merchant migrate after the Sendlane acquisition?",
    "answer": "Ownership alone is not a migration trigger. Confirm your account plan and compare the supported capture, email and SMS setup with the workflow you need."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can we keep Privy forms?",
    "answer": "Consider retaining capture if it works. First demonstrate that fields, permission evidence and updates reach the receiving system without duplicate enrollment or overwriting withdrawals."
  },
  {
    "question": "What makes a replacement acceptable?",
    "answer": "Accept field and identity mappings, capture behavior, purchase exits, permission changes and queue ownership before enabling customer sends. Reconcile actual sends before rollback."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a recovery discount preserve margin?",
    "answer": "Not automatically. In the illustrative $234 cart with 46% gross margin, a 15% discount reduces contribution from $107.64 to $72.54 with goods cost fixed, before other variable costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16 container">
<a href="/alternatives" class="link">← All alternatives</a>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-10">
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Privy alternatives: preserve capture while changing recovery</h1>
<h2>Start with the capture and sending boundary</h2>
<p>Privy can be more than a popup supplier. Its <a href="https://www.privy.com/changelog">current changelog</a> documents email and SMS Flows, display updates and preference management. Connected capture and sending can reduce the work of maintaining separate tools. Keep that benefit in the comparison: if the problem is a field mapping or an overlapping journey, repair it before replacing the account.</p>
<p>Checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://www.privy.com/blog/privy-acquires-sendlane">Privy announced its acquisition of Sendlane</a> in February 2026. That announcement describes continued investment in connected onsite, email and SMS marketing; it does not establish automatic account transfer or a shutdown. Request your account-specific access, billing, support and transition plan rather than treating a corporate announcement as a cutover instruction.</p>
<h2>Choose what to retain before choosing another tool</h2>
<p>List the actual gap: a display that interrupts mobile checkout, missing capture fields, a recovery branch you cannot express, or conflicting senders. Compare staying and repairing, retaining Privy capture with a separate sender, and replacing both capture and sending. A separate sender may let the team own its desired recovery logic, but adds a data boundary that needs an accountable operator.</p>
<p>Use <a href="/alternatives/klaviyo-alternative">Klaviyo</a>, <a href="/alternatives/omnisend-alternative">Omnisend</a> or <a href="/alternatives/recart-alternative">Recart</a> as candidate evaluation paths, not ranked winners. If considering <a href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy</a> for a lifecycle proposal, require a demonstration of your Shopify events, capture handoff and suppression behavior. Select the proposal whose operator can maintain the required workflow and whose total cost fits the store.</p>
<h2>Build a field, identity and caller register</h2>
<p>Inventory active popups, embedded forms, checkout capture, imports, API callers and integrations. For each, record its storefront location, destination, field names and types, customer identifier, email or phone normalization, permission purpose and source timestamp. Distinguish an incentive preference from permission to send. A phone number without an email needs an explicit mapping; a shared email alone should not merge different people.</p>
<p>Assign one writer for each permission field and document how conflicts resolve. Preserve withdrawals, topic preferences and suppressions with their evidence. A later form submission or Shopify profile update must not silently restore a withdrawn subscription. Reconcile sendable, suppressed and unresolved records separately; an equal import count does not prove that the receiving system can make the same eligibility decision.</p>
<h2>Rehearse capture continuity</h2>
<p>These are proposed acceptance exercises, not observed vendor tests. Submit a new mobile signup, a returning subscriber, a phone-only profile and a withdrawn contact who updates an address. Inspect the resulting identity, consent evidence and intended welcome or recovery entry in a non-sending environment. Change a form field and trace which caller updates it. Reject duplicate enrollment, missing evidence or an unexplained permission overwrite.</p>
<p>If retaining forms, have the receiving operator demonstrate a failed handoff, its retry record and a safe replay. If replacing forms, check display targeting, close controls, incentive delivery, page performance and the removal of old scripts. Keep capture active through an explicitly owned path; do not leave two incentive forms competing for the same shopper.</p>
<h2>Turn merchant friction into useful recovery checks</h2>
<p>For a distracted mobile shopper, verify that the return link restores the intended cart without exposing another customer’s details. For a financing interruption, check that copy explains supported payment choices without promising approval. For shipping shock, show the actual delivery terms before proposing a code. These cases test useful assistance rather than assuming every abandonment needs a discount.</p>
<p>For gift sizing, retain the chosen variant and an accurate sizing or exchange link. For an unavailable variant, suppress the stale offer or provide an approved alternative. For minimum-order restrictions, explain the requirement without implying that a coupon removes it. Test an existing promotion against a recovery code and a repeat purchaser against first-order incentives; the eligible offer must match checkout behavior.</p>
<h2>Reconcile queues, purchases and rollback</h2>
<p>Record which system owns every scheduled campaign and recovery action, including welcome and SMS collisions. Pause the outgoing sender and reconcile queued work before activating the replacement. Map store, customer, checkout, order and stable event identifiers. Immediately before each send decision, check current purchase, inventory, permission and suppression state; an old abandonment event is insufficient.</p>
<p>Propose a duplicate event, a delayed purchase, a withdrawal after enrollment and an out-of-order replay. Keep an idempotency record scoped to store, purpose and intended action so the replay does not recreate an already processed message. Choose send delays and contact pressure from your journey and observed event latency. To roll back, pause the new queue, reconcile sends and new withdrawals, then restore only eligible unsent actions under one owner.</p>
<h2>Compare contribution and operating effort</h2>
<p>Illustrative economics, not a Privy result: a $234 cart at 46% gross margin has $126.36 goods cost and $107.64 full-price contribution. A 15% discount makes revenue $198.90 and contribution $72.54 with goods cost fixed, reducing contribution by $35.10. Add messaging, platform, shipping, returns and implementation costs separately. Evaluate incremental orders against a suitable comparison group rather than treating attributed revenue as recovered profit.</p>
<p>Request quotes using your actual contact mix, channel usage and service needs. Include form rebuilding, integration maintenance and ongoing permission reconciliation. Accept the change when the merchant cases and ownership records pass review, not after an arbitrary number of weeks. Keep Privy when its supported configuration meets these requirements with less operating work.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="FAQ: Privy alternatives" />
</section>
</BaseLayout>
